Typical Instruments
- Rhythm Electric Guitar: Heavily modified solid-body electric guitars (often with passive ceramic humbuckers) tuned to D-Standard or Drop-C, dialed for razor-sharp pick attack and dry mid-range crunch.
- Space & Orbital Processors: Eventide DSP racks, algorithmic shimmer pedals, and customized convolution reverbs loaded with impulse responses from satellite dishes and decompression chambers.
- Drums: Hybrid acoustic-electronic thrash kit featuring deep Birch shells, reinforced steel snare, rapid-fire triggers, and high-pitch Paiste cymbals that cut through atmospheric soup.
- Synthesizers: Modular Eurorack ambient systems producing slowly evolving drone beds, interstellar radiotelescope tone generators, and glass-like wavetable pads.

